  "summary": "Today's health-tech headlines reveal several major themes shaping the sector. AI governance and validation are emerging as critical challenges as healthcare organizations scale artificial intelligence deployments—both Epic and Pearl Health are expanding AI platforms for providers, while healthcare CIOs are grappling with hallucinations and trust issues that require new validation frameworks. Digital health infrastructure is advancing globally, with Italy scaling nationwide digital health initiatives and regional healthcare networks gaining prominence as a transformation model, complemented by Epic's growing international EHR market share. On the policy front, significant shifts are underway: the Trump administration is pursuing ambitious changes to federal research oversight and grant authority, while RFK Jr. plans to create a list of vaccine-related injuries and officials are pushing to onshore generic drug manufacturing. Finally, healthcare economics remain turbulent as ACA insurers seek double-digit premium increases for the second consecutive year amid rising costs and policy changes, and a major nursing strike at Massachusetts General Brigham continues amid failed contract negotiations. Separately, novel clinical applications are emerging, including transplant success for stage 4 lung cancer patients and FDA approval of an OTC continuous glucose monitor for young children, though each raises important clinical questions.",
